      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-19T16:40:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You need this CL, which recently landed: https://crrev.com/c/3901254",
      "parentUuid": "9e11ba58_01e0214d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 7,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "a61feb58f50eb882f77cfa0ab65caccd2f35fa74",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "32ca93b7_38b0441b",
        "filename": "core/host/toolchain.mk",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 7,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-19T16:46:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Another option would be to set `CROSS_COMPILE_host\u003d`, which would probably match the way it\u0027s done for `arm` better.\n\nI think any empty variable won\u0027t work with the existing definition for [`set-option`](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/c696435b768ccff0be01e916b799be030fefd0fd/Makefile.toolchain#231). You\u0027d probably need to modify it to check that the variable is `undefined` like [this](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/c696435b768ccff0be01e916b799be030fefd0fd/Makefile.toolchain#55).",
      "parentUuid": "13555687_58ed7e4c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 7,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "a61feb58f50eb882f77cfa0ab65caccd2f35fa74",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8ec68c47_b6335775",
        "filename": "core/host/toolchain.mk",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 7,
      "author": {
        "id": 1483403
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-19T19:05:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, after crrev/c/3901254 I did get this command to work:\n\nmake -j$(nproc) CRYPTOC_DIR\u003d\"${MODULES_DIR}/cryptoc\" CROSS_COMPILE_arm\u003d/opt/zephyr-sdk/arm-zephyr-eabi/bin/arm-zephyr-eabi- CROSS_COMPILE_host\u003d/usr/bin/ test-coverage\n\nAnd that has nice symmetry.",
      "parentUuid": "32ca93b7_38b0441b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 7,
        "endChar": 24
      },
